The loop that sets the offsets for unused color planes was removed when the number of potential color planes increased to 4. This led to the situation where the offsets for unused planes were not being set to `~0xfff`, allowing stale auxiliary surface offsets to be used in calculations, which could result in incorrect positioning of the main surface relative to the auxiliary surface.

